Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:10:38 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 206/230] feat(feed): 7-day strip and calendar button in the
 header
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The strip's own 44px calendar button made the row read as eight uneven
targets and pushed the last chip past the cards' edge at 390px, while the
clipped first chip was the scroll container eating its own gutter.

The strip is now one row of seven equal chips spanning exactly the content
width, with the window (yesterday..today+5) re-centring on a date picked
outside it. The calendar moved up next to refresh as a 40px circle with a
44px hit band, and the sheet gained a "Today" shortcut.

